    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="1078" n="944" xml:id="pg944"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/6–3045: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 622<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Washington Liaison Representative for
                        the Delegation to the Allied Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wolf</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Representative
                        on the Allied Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pauley</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d622-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-30T14:00:00-04:00">June 30, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1473. For Pauley from Wolf.</p>
                <p> Ralph Davies PAW advises from best information available his Program Division
                    indicated 1946 surplus petroleum supplies in eastern European areas under
                    Russian occupation will be approximately 60,000 BD over local requirements.
                    Romania accounts [for] 47,000 BD this figure. At same time he advises imports
                    from Anglo-American sources to meet requirements western and Mediterranean
                    Europe will average approximately 292,000 BD last half [19]45 and 226,000 BD
                    [19]46. Any utilization apparent surplus eastern Europe not only eases critical
                    petroleum supply condition world wide but effects material transportation saving
                    if movement to western and Mediterranean Europe overland or from Constanta by
                    tanker initiated promptly. Sending under separate cover Davies letter and
                    supporting tables.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d622-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
